cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the article and this repository."
title: "Phase-dependent transient feasibility and buffer sizing of a shared-pole four-port AC/DC converter with digital-twin validation: code, models and results"
abstract: "Code, models and results for the article of the same title. In a converter whose energy buffer shares a switching pole with two AC ports, whether a load step can be survived depends on the AC phase at which it arrives. The repository holds the averaged and switched converter models, the linear-programming feasibility bounds, the Simscape Electrical cross-check, the reproduction of a published experiment, the digital-twin validation and the campaigns behind every figure and table, with their predeclared protocols and results. Code: MIT licence. Data, figures and documents: CC BY 4.0 (see DATA_LICENSE.md)."
